<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-HOIUPANK TO INCREASE 1997 FORECAST.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-HOIUPANK TO INCREASE 1997 FORECAST.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, the second largest bank in Estonia, said on Tuesday that it was calculating a new, higher profit forecast for 1997.</p>
<p>The bank earlier forecast its net profit for 1997 at 113 million kroons at the start of the year.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are calculating a new forecast...which will be ready rather soon,&quot; Juta Maar, Hoiupank board member, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Maar did not say what the new profit figure will be but said it will be higher than the previous estimate.</p>
<p>Hoiupank started to revise its 1997 profit forecast already in April, she added.</p>
<p>Hoiupank earlier reported a net profit of 58 million kroons in the first four months of this year, over half of the present profit forecast.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
